n Tajikistan until 1933, when Ismoil Somoni Peak (known as "Stalin Peak" at the time) was climbed and found to be more than 300 metres higher.","title":"Lenin Peak"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Two mountains in the Pamirs in China, Kongur Tagh (7,649 m) and Muztagh Ata (7,546 m), are higher than the Tajik summits.","title":"Lenin Peak"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Rush Peak is a mountain in the Karakoram mountain range of Central Asia.","title":"Rush Peak"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is located in the Nagar District of Gilgit-Baltistan, Pakistan.","title":"Rush Peak"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" While not a high peak by local standards, it is noteworthy as a remote trekking destination.","title":"Rush Peak"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" It can be reached via Nagar Valley and Hoper Village.","title":"Rush Peak"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The peak can be accessed via Hoper Glacier (Bualtar Glacier) and Barpu Glacier.","title":"Rush Peak"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The peak is relatively easy to climb in the summer months and ascents have been made by amateur climbers without proper mountaineering gear.","title":"Rush Peak"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" In winter, access to the mountain is made difficult by heavy snows.","title":"Rush Peak"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" The top of the peak provides stunning views of Miar Peak (6,824 m), Miar Glacier and Phuparash Peak (6,574 m).","title":"Rush Peak"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" On a clear day, one can look east and see some of the world's highest mountains, including K2 and Broad Peak.","title":"Rush Peak"},{"sentence_id":9,"text":" At the mountain's base lies one of the world's highest alpine lakes, Rush Lake (4,694m).","title":"Rush Peak"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Karakoram, or Karakorum is a large mountain range spanning the borders of Pakistan, India, and China, with the northwest extremity of the range extending to Afghanistan and Tajikistan.","title":"Karakoram"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is located in the regions of Gilgit–Baltistan (Pakistan), Ladakh (India), and southern Xinjiang (China), and reaches the Wakhan Corridor (Afghanistan).","title":"Karakoram"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" A part of the complex of ranges from the Hindu Kush to the Himalayan Range, it is one of the Greater Ranges of Asia.","title":"Karakoram"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The Karakoram is home to the four most closely located peaks over 8000m in height on earth: K2, the second highest peak in the world at 8611 m , Gasherbrum I, Broad Peak and Gasherbrum II.","title":"Karakoram"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Broad Peak (Urdu: ‎ ) is the 12th highest mountain in the world at 8051 m above sea level.","title":"Broad Peak"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The literal translation of "Broad Peak" to Falchan Kangri (ཨིྰན་ཨངརི་) is not accepted among the Balti people.","title":"Broad Peak"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The English name was introduced in 1892 by the British explorer Martin Conway, in reference to the similarly named Breithorn in the Alps.","title":"Broad Peak"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Broad Peak is higher.
